krdpserver refuses a client without a pointer cache, where it crashed.
krdp sends a client the pointer's shape through the client's pointer
cache, and means to refuse a client that advertises none (pointer
cache size 0): "Client doesn't support pointer caching, aborting". But
that check runs in the Capabilities callback, which FreeRDP calls
before the server's Demand Active, on the server's own settings; the
client's size comes with its Confirm Active. So the check never fires,
the client is accepted, and the first cursor image evicts from an empty
cache in Cursor::update and crashes the server. The check moves to
Activate, where the client's capabilities have been applied.

This is the commit proposed to upstream KRdp (branch
pointer-cache-check of curiousj/krdp on invent.kde.org, made against
master), unchanged; it applies to krdp 6.8.2 as it is. It goes when
the krdp built has it. krdp-embed-cursor.patch applies on top and
turns the refusal into a pointer painted into the video.

diff --git a/src/RdpConnection.cpp b/src/RdpConnection.cpp
index 8e46a81..541cf14 100644
--- a/src/RdpConnection.cpp
+++ b/src/RdpConnection.cpp
@@ -626,11 +626,6 @@ bool RdpConnection::onCapabilities()
         freerdp_settings_set_uint32(settings, FreeRDP_ColorDepth, 32);
     }
 
-    if (freerdp_settings_get_uint32(settings,FreeRDP_PointerCacheSize) <= 0) {
-        qCWarning(KRDP) << "Client doesn't support pointer caching, aborting";
-        return false;
-    }
-
     return true;
 }
 
@@ -656,6 +651,14 @@ static std::optional<quint8> qualitySeedForConnectionType(uint32_t connectionTyp
 
 bool RdpConnection::onActivate()
 {
+    // The client's pointer cache size arrives with its Confirm Active, which
+    // answers the Demand Active sent after onCapabilities(); until then the
+    // setting holds the server's own default. Cursor relies on a cache.
+    if (freerdp_settings_get_uint32(d->peer->context->settings, FreeRDP_PointerCacheSize) == 0) {
+        qCWarning(KRDP) << "Client doesn't support pointer caching, aborting";
+        return false;
+    }
+
     setState(State::Activated);
 
     if (!d->qualitySeeded) {
